Wine & Spirits","shared_category_count":6},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Cajun/Creole, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Nightlife","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1}],"text":[{"business_id":"lK-YaoQ670dGJrmaqyJTBA","review_id":"ChVDnnRAeWo_vSK63Di8IA","date":"2011-07-01T21:11:25","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9326801300048828,"text_excerpt":"This is a really cool place to grab a drink(or five) after work, since it also has a kitchen -hours and days are limited, though. They have happy hour specials but I never make it down here early enough so I'm forced to pay full price. Bummer, because I know places with all-around service industry discounts... But, the beer selection is pretty good and reasonably priced and the food is really tasty. Btw, they really did a great job fixing this place up a few years ago, the interior looks great!"},{"business_id":"lK-YaoQ670dGJrmaqyJTBA","review_id":"X6AGEUOINmUMgp3ar_RK8Q","date":"2013-04-24T13:09:43","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9306762218475342,"text_excerpt":"This is a super solid spot in the Fulton street area of town. The bar is very attentive and good at their job of keeping a drink in your hand. The service is always friendly and efficient. The big shocker to me about this place is the food. It's really pretty good! I recommend the fried shrimp po-boy. They have a great batter that is crispy with a touch of spice. Ernst is a friendly, well lit, smoke-free bar, with decent food in an area of the city that is not really known for any of those things. A great place to stop in for a drink or hang out for hours with your friends. Highly recommended."},{"business_id":"lK-YaoQ670dGJrmaqyJTBA","review_id":"eJfzoWVS1XYtBG1hvY0mOw","date":"2011-02-05T04:08:15","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9279689788818359,"text_excerpt":"This place is awesome! It doesn't close til 6 AM. Bartender is nice and friendly, regardless of the time of night you are there. They serve both beer and mixed drinks. Kitchen closes at 11 on weekdays, but I'm not sure about weekends. I also came here for a private party upstairs with FREE FOOD AND UNLIMITED BEER!!! How can a girl pass that up?! A few things on the menu were: 1) COCONUT BATTERED LOBSTERS (I'm not sure I saw these go by) 2) CRAWFISH EGGROLLS (they were delicious) 3) BEEF HIBACHI SKEWERS 4) BACON WRAPPED SHRIMP PUFFS (my friend ate a ton of these! and the waitress was so nice to just keep coming back to him to clear her tray!) 5) SEAFOOD STUFFED MUSHROOMS (it tasted a tad w..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"lK-YaoQ670dGJrmaqyJTBA","photo_id":"zYa8i25ffYuREJGTa0PTpg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/zYa8i25ffYuREJGTa0PTpg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8660714030265808},{"business_id":"lK-YaoQ670dGJrmaqyJTBA","photo_id":"DRSMcU2js0CX5hHzXEOABA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/DRSMcU2js0CX5hHzXEOA